<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Zoutpansberg Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1849 CE – 1864 CE (approx.) · capital Schoemansdal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A remote Boer republic in the far northern Transvaal built around the ivory-hunting town of Schoemansdal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a> led his followers north from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrigstad">Ohrigstad</a> in 1848 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soutpansberg">Soutpansberg</a> mountains, where they founded the village later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a>. After Potgieter's death in 1852 the community was led by his son Piet and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephanus-schoeman">Stephanus Schoeman</a>, and it acted as a separate republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a> lived mainly from elephant hunting and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inhambane">Inhambane</a>, using African hunters armed with guns. Its government was a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> and commandants. Relations with the neighbouring <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venda-kingdom">Venda Kingdom</a> were tense, with raids, labour exactions and the capture of children for service.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soutpansberg">Zoutpansberg</a> was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a> in the early 1860s. As elephants were hunted out and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venda-people">Venda</a> resistance grew, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a> abandoned and burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a> in 1867.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1849 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.50%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1849 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schoemansdal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andries Hendrik Potgieter, Stephanus Schoeman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zoutpansberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=zoutpansberg-republic" aria-label="Zoutpansberg Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5475 3028 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zoutpansberg Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5795 3284L5746 3380"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5746 3380h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5795 3284h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5795 3284h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schoemansdal. <a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=zoutpansberg-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
